target: internal/record/record.go
verify: go test ./internal/record/ -count=1 -run 'TestConvergenceRules'
expect: a_cycle_with_no_agents_field_spends_nothing
why:    a cycle row with NO `agents` key spends nothing, which is the Python's `or 0`. 17 of the real store's cycle rows omit it, so reading absence as one inflates the spend on most runs and can push a run over its cap. Now anchored on AgentsSpent, the ONE place the rule lives: before the extraction it was written out three times (Convergence, Disclosure, push.Fingerprint) and this entry pinned only one of them, so the other two could have been edited without the catalog noticing — which is the duplication the extraction removed.
--- old
		if c.Agents != nil {
			n += *c.Agents
		}
--- new
		if c.Agents == nil {
			n++
		} else {
			n += *c.Agents
		}
